joplin-terminal provides the official Joplin Terminal (Joplin CLI Client),
version 3.7.1, installed under tools/joplin-terminal/.

Launchers
  Linux/macOS: tools/joplin-terminal/joplin
  Windows:     tools/joplin-terminal/joplin.cmd

Runtime requirement
  The launchers use the system Node.js from PATH. The bundled native addons
  (keytar, sqlite3, sharp) use Node-API, which is ABI-stable across Node.js
  major versions, so the runtime Node does not need to match the build-time
  Node. Node 18.17+ is recommended (required by sharp); Joplin itself only
  requires Node 10+. The launcher prints a clear error if node is not found.
  On Linux, keytar also needs libsecret-1 at runtime for the system keyring.

Common commands
  joplin version
  joplin help
  joplin sync
  joplin server start     # local Data API / Web Clipper service
  joplin server status
  joplin server stop

The first launch creates the profile in ~/.config/joplin (Linux),
~/Library/Application Support/joplin (macOS), or %USERPROFILE%\.config\joplin
(Windows).

Build note
  Native addons are built for the host OS and architecture, so Windows and
  macOS triplets must be built on a matching host. Different linkage triplets
  on the same OS/architecture (for example x64-osx-dynamic on an x64-osx host)
  are fine; the port refuses only a genuinely different host OS or
  architecture. npm installs transitive dependencies at build time, so the
  build machine needs network access.
  At build time the port first checks any Node.js already on PATH: it must run
  and satisfy ^18.17.0 || ^20.3.0 || >=21.0.0 (sharp's requirement). Unusable
  candidates are reported and skipped. Only when no system Node qualifies does
  the port download Node 22.23.5 on demand into buildtrees; no vcpkg Node
  package is installed unconditionally.
